### 3.1 Preliminary: Ridge Regression

Toner and Darlow [20](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2606.27282#bib.bib20) showed that recent linear forecasting variants are functionally equivalent to unconstrained linear regression over appropriately augmented feature sets. We take this unification as our starting point and build on the simple and efficient setup: Ridge regression [10](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2606.27282#bib.bib10) with a closed-form solution. Given a context window 𝐱∈ℝL\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{L} of LL past observations for a single variate and a forecast horizon HH, the model predicts 𝐲^=𝐖𝐱+𝐛\hat{\mathbf{y}}=\mathbf{W}\mathbf{x}+\mathbf{b} where 𝐖∈ℝH×L\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{H\times L} and 𝐛∈ℝH\mathbf{b}\in\mathbb{R}^{H}. The weight matrix is obtained by solving

